From fb7bff878ddef17c2ea5e6be80a86402bf9ed35f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 12:01:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03253/11362] [outer-loop] arc3_live_submit: replay the CURRENT
 validated package, not the stale 13-level set

The live-submit driver hardcoded the 11-game/13-level set frozen at the 2026-06-17 FIRST
submission. Since then reproducible_total_levels grew 13 -> 52 and the conductor prepared a
validated 45-level package (exp4473), but the submit COMMAND would still replay only the old
13 -- leaving ~26 reproduced levels on the table at submit time.

_build_claimed() now sources {game: levels} dynamically from the newest
results/experiment_*submission_package*.json manifest (auto-tracking conductor refreshes),
intersected with the games the metaharness can actually replay (non-empty banked trajectory).
Drops env-unmatched and graph-explore-only games (no replayable action sequence). Falls back
to the preserved CLAIMED_FALLBACK (the 2026-06-17 set) when no package is found -- never empty.

Offline-verified: the driver now replays 16 games / 39 claimed levels (lp85=5, sc25=5, tu93=5,
tn36=7, tr87=6, ...) vs the prior 11 games / 13 levels. Submission stays operator-only: the
validate-first flow (no --submit) surfaces any live env-mismatch before the irreversible close.

This is submission-PREP only -- it does NOT submit. Operator runs validate, then --submit.

